<div class="tray-title-small">
<span>Character Sheet</span>
{{!--
    The mode switch: favourites, the sheet, and compendium quick-add.

    The heart and the person are always both here. Favourites is a view now
    rather than a block pinned above the tabs, so there is always somewhere to
    switch back FROM -- which is why the person icon is no longer gated behind
    `canUseCompendiums` the way it was when the pair was a two-state switch and
    the second state was compendiums. A player who cannot browse compendiums
    still gets two modes and needs both icons to move between them.

    The broom is not one of them and keeps its separator: it opens a window that
    writes to the sheet, rather than changing what this column shows.
--}}
<div class="control-mode-toggles">
    {{#if canCleanup}}
    <i class="fa-solid fa-broom control-cleanup" title="{{cleanupTooltip}}"></i>
    <span class="control-toggle-separator"></span>
    {{/if}}
    <i class="fa-solid fa-heart control-mode-toggle" data-mode="favorites" title="Show Favorites"></i>
    <i class="fa-solid fa-user control-mode-toggle" data-mode="sheet" title="Show This Character's Items"></i>
    {{#if canUseCompendiums}}
    <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass control-mode-toggle" data-mode="search" title="{{compendiumToggleTitle}}"></i>
    {{/if}}
</div>
</div>
<div class="control-search">
<input type="text" class="global-search" placeholder="Search All Sections...">
<i class="fa-solid fa-times search-clear" title="Clear Search"></i>
</div>
{{#if canAddFromCompendiums}}
<label class="control-search-option" title="On: adding empties the search box and stays here, for adding several things. Off: adding returns to the character sheet and scrolls to the new item.">
<input type="checkbox" class="compendium-clear-on-add" {{#if clearOnAdd}}checked{{/if}}>
<span>Clear search and keep open on add</span>
</label>
{{/if}}
{{!--
    SECTION TABS

    These were five chips, and the chips were a multi-select whose common use was
    single-select. That is the whole reason they are tabs now: five chips can all
    be off at once, and "I filtered away the thing I was looking for" was mostly
    that. A tab has no off state, so the item-type dimension can no longer be
    narrowed to nothing, and where you are is a lit label rather than an
    inference from which of five icons is not dimmed.

    Favorites is not among them. It is a flag rather than an item kind, so it was
    never the same axis -- it sits above whichever tab is open, always shown.

    Five text labels need room: the tray's minimum width is 400px for this strip
    and nothing else. See SQUIRE.TRAY_MIN_WIDTH.
--}}
<div class="control-tabs">
{{#each tabs}}
<button class="control-tab{{#if active}} active{{/if}}" data-tab="{{key}}">{{label}}</button>
{{/each}}
</div>
{{!--
    THE FILTER BAR

    What survived. Five action chips, and the two availability toggles.

    Every chip names a bucket and a row hides when its bucket is off; a row in no
    bucket is untouched. Every row has at least one action cost -- Passive is
    what guarantees it -- so turning all five off empties the tray, which is the
    same "you can filter this to nothing" hazard the type chips had. It stays
    here because five chips you set this session and that reset on reload is a
    different animal from nine that persisted for a week.

    The availability toggles are the four equipped/unequipped/prepared/unprepared
    chips collapsed back into two questions with two answers each: show all, or
    show only the usable ones. That loses "what am I carrying but not wearing",
    which the four-chip split existed to make askable -- a real question, a rare
    one, and worth the trade for two controls that read at a glance.

    Which toggles appear depends on the open tab, but what they MEAN never does:
    the flags are global. Weapons and Inventory share the equipped flag; Spells
    owns prepared; Feats can answer neither so it shows none; All shows both and
    is therefore the one place the whole filter state is legible.
--}}
<div class="control-filter-bar">
<div class="filter-group">
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-a filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="action" data-tooltip="Costs an action"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-b filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="bonus" data-tooltip="Costs a bonus action"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-r filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="reaction" data-tooltip="Costs a reaction"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-s filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="special" data-tooltip="Special activation"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-p filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="passive" data-tooltip="Costs no turn action — gear, passives, and anything slower than a turn"></i>
</div>
<span class="filter-separator"></span>
<div class="filter-group filter-group-availability">
<button class="availability-toggle" data-availability="equipped" data-tooltip="Only equipped gear. Says nothing about spells or features, and applies on both the Weapons and Inventory tabs." hidden>
<i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i><span>Equipped</span>
</button>
<button class="availability-toggle" data-availability="prepared" data-tooltip="Only prepared spells, plus cantrips and anything always available. Says nothing about gear." hidden>
<i class="fa-solid fa-sun"></i><span>Prepared</span>
</button>
</div>
</div>
